WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.604
This equation describes any sine. It has four numbers: the amplitude A, the angular frequency omega, the initial phase phi and the DC offset C.

2
00:00:10.247 --> 00:00:17.226
A is the peak amplitude: the distance from the center of the wave to its maximum. If it doubles, the wave grows twice as tall.

3
00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:25.795
C is the mean value, or DC offset: it moves the whole curve up or down. It is not heard, but it takes headroom away before clipping.

4
00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:32.714
Omega is the angular frequency: how many radians the cycle covers per second. It is two pi times the frequency.

5
00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:40.789
Phi is the initial phase: at which point of the cycle the wave starts. Ninety degrees are pi over two radians, a quarter turn.
